{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur woke to the scent of pine and damp earth, a smell he'd always associated with his grandfather's cabin. But something felt…off. The sunlight streaming through the window wasn't the golden hue of a normal morning; it was pixelated, shimmering with an unnatural clarity. He reached out to touch the rough-hewn wood of the wall, and his fingers passed right through it. Panic flared as he looked down. His worn flannel shirt wasn’t his own; it was a tunic of some sort of fantasy adventurer, stitched with gleaming silver thread. He tried to sit up, and his limbs felt strangely…rigid, like they were powered by hydraulics. A nearby wooden table displayed a gleaming sword and a leather-bound journal, their textures impossibly detailed. This wasn't his cabin. This wasn't his life. He was inside a video game.\n\n***\n\nA wave of disorientation washed over him, followed by a chilling realization. The forest around him wasn't just scenery; it *reacted* to his movements. A nearby rabbit bolted, its fur rendered with hyperrealistic detail. He instinctively reached for the sword, and it felt impossibly solid in his hand. A faint HUD shimmered into existence in his vision, displaying stats like \"Health: 100/100\" and \"Stamina: 50/50\". He was a character, a player, trapped within the code of a meticulously crafted world. The journal felt heavy in his grasp, filled with cryptic entries and quest descriptions. He had no idea what his purpose was, or how to escape, but one thing was certain: his life had just become a whole lot more complicated.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁woke", "logprob": -1.7583379745483398}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.48595893383026123}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.0051826415583491325}, {"token": "▁scent", "logprob": -2.720264434814453}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁pine